cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnuLM in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "AnuLM: a small, trainable mixture-of-experts language model in the shape of Sarvam 30B, trained from scratch on one GPU for Hindi, English and Python"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MOBIRIZER-TECHNOLOGY/AnuLM"
url: "https://huggingface.co/<hf-owner>"
authors:
  - name: "The AnuLM authors"
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - Hindi
  - Indic languages
  - small language model
  - code generation
  - machine translation
abstract: >-
  AnuLM (अणु, "atom") is an independent re-implementation of the Sarvam 30B
  architecture (grouped-query attention, 24 routed experts with aux-loss-free
  balancing, sliding-window attention on the lower layers) at roughly 400M
  parameters, 174M active per token, in pure PyTorch. It ships the training,
  evaluation and serving code, the data recipes, and three checkpoints
  trained on a single consumer GPU: a Python coder (MBPP 12.5% pass@1), an
  English-Hindi translator (chrF 41.5 / 43.4 on FLORES-200 devtest) and a
  Hindi/English question answerer. The project is not affiliated with Sarvam
  AI, BharatGen, AI4Bharat or the Government of India.
